          {
            "commit": "e4ab0a76f12496fc0e02216a2c34e6414c09fff8",
            "subject": "LU-20438 lnd: Add lnd_get_device callback for LND modules"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Shivaji Kant",
          "email": "shivajikant@google.com",
          "date": "2026-08-07 09:38:20.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Shivaji Kant",
          "email": "shivajikant@google.com",
          "date": "2026-08-28 16:27:25.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20438 lnet: Implement distance-based PCIe P2PDMA routing",
        "message": "LU-20438 lnet: Implement distance-based PCIe P2PDMA routing\n\nThis patch completes the P2P hardware distance topology abstraction,\nvastly optimizing network interface (NI) selection for GPUDirect RDMA.\n\nBy introducing the lnd_get_device callback on the LND, LNet statically\nqueries and evaluates the physical PCIe distance between the GPU\n(page provider) and all active host configuration adapters (HCAs).\nThis ensures LNet bounds multi-rail transfers to perfectly matched NICs\ncollocated beneath the identical PCIe switch, sidestepping NUMA traffic.\n\nAlso includes robust m4 autotools validation to failover gracefully\nto NUMA routing on legacy infrastructures lacking PCIe p2pdma heuristics.\n\nChange-Id: I86e51f55028af7e83b4383f5a2ae3b8bd4051fda\nSigned-off-by: Shivaji Kant <shivajikant@google.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
